    "verdict": "Under convention D the corpus places the theory in the Temperley-Lieb quotient, and descent is annihilation of the ideal, so the Q_beta ansatz has exactly TWO admissible functionals -- the augmentation, which is the UNIQUE surviving multiplicative one (H_3 has two 1-dim reps and the other IS the quotiented block), and the Markov trace at z_D. Both give determined numbers, and they BRACKET the measured Q-value: augmentation 12.4700 %, trace -43.1571 %. The coordinate sum the ansatz actually evaluates reproduces Q_codata to 0.16775 % and is INADMISSIBLE. So the functional that matches experiment is precisely the one the canonical convention forbids, and both permitted ones miss by more than an order of magnitude in opposite directions. Reported plainly as evidence against the ansatz as it stands. The bracket means some convex combination hits the target exactly; that is a one-parameter fit against a single anchor, it is NOT computed here, and any future weight must be derived from the representation rather than read off Q_codata. Scope-(a); nothing wired."
